# CANONICAL §7.3 fixture — OffsetFace `resultPolicyVersion: 3`, the BLEND-AWARE
# reading (WP3-C5). What it pins is IDENTITY across a suppress → offset → reblend
# chain, which is the part of V3 that is a cross-track contract rather than a
# kernel result.
#
# Model: 10 x 10 rect extruded 10, then ONE vertical edge filleted R2. Pushing a
# SUPPORT wall of that fillet is the case V2 gets wrong — V2 sweeps the whole G1
# closure, so the fillet inflates and the second wall is dragged along. V3 reads
# the SAME stored pair (`faceIds` = the frozen closure, `primaryFaceIds` = the
# user's pick) as "move the pick, suppress the blend, rebuild it at its measured
# radius", so only the picked wall moves.
#
# The stored operative set here is exactly the blend-aware closure of the pick:
# the pushed wall, the blend, and the blend's other support. A stored set that no
# longer closes over the picks is refused `OFFSET_FACE_CLOSURE_MISMATCH` — V3
# checks that in BOTH directions, where V2 only checked one.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXTURE PINS
#   * a single `modified` event on the target — an offset never fans a body out;
#   * the suppressed-then-recreated BLEND FACE KEEPS ITS ElementId, arriving as
#     `elementMapDelta.relabeled`. The lineage is asserted in the worker exactly
#     where the reblend reproduction proof passed; without it the face would fall
#     to the generic descriptor+anchor ladder with no blend-specific evidence at
#     all, which is a rebind on weaker grounds, not a refusal;
#   * the blend's two boundary edges are genuinely consumed and land in
#     `elementMapDelta.removed`. They are NOT synthesized onto a successor — an
#     edge the offset splits has no unique correspondence and V1 refuses to guess,
#     so they fall to the confidence-gated ladder like any other lost element.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXTURE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT PIN: any geometry number. The whole
# point of V3 is a different VOLUME for the same request (V3 1191.4159265358979
# vs V2 1405.6637061435916 on this exact body), and `json_subset` compares numbers
# EXACTLY — an NDJSON exchange is the wrong instrument for a measured quantity.
# Those live where they are measurable: worker/tests/test_offsetface_reblend.cpp.
# `offset_face_v2_unchanged.ndjson` is the same model and the same push at
# version 2, so the two files pin the IDENTITY difference between the readings.
# Same boundary as circular_pattern_lineage.ndjson's step angle.
#
# HARNESS SEMANTICS worth knowing before adding an assertion here: `json_subset`
# matches an expected array as a POSITIONAL PREFIX of the actual one, so an
# expected `[]` matches ANY array and asserts nothing. Emptiness is therefore
# never claimed by writing `[]`; it is proved positively, with a `QueryElement`
# whose `present` is the fact in question.
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"hello","seq":0}}
{"send":{"v":1,"t":"req","id":1,"verb":"OpenSession","args":{"documentId":"doc_offset_face_v3","documentRevision":0,"workerEpoch":4,"mode":"determinism"}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"resp","id":1,"ok":true,"result":{"sessionOpen":true}}}
# The seed model. The fillet's edge is addressed by ANCHOR evidence (the ladder's
# lowest rung) because nothing is bound yet — ElementIds are Rust's to mint.
{"send":{"v":1,"t":"req","id":2,"verb":"ExecutePlan","args":{"jobId":31,"documentRevision":1,"workerEpoch":4,"expectedBaseHash":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","prefixHashes":["aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa","bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb","cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc"],"targetStep":2,"ops":[{"opType":"Sketch","opId":"op0","stepIndex":0,"params":{"sketchId":"sk1","plane":{"kind":"XY"},"entities":[{"id":"e1","type":"Line","p0":[0,0],"p1":[10,0]},{"id":"e2","type":"Line","p0":[10,0],"p1":[10,10]},{"id":"e3","type":"Line","p0":[10,10],"p1":[0,10]},{"id":"e4","type":"Line","p0":[0,10],"p1":[0,0]}],"constraints":[]}},{"opType":"Extrude","opId":"op1","stepIndex":1,"inputs":[{"primary":{"bodyId":"","elementId":"sk1.region.r0","kind":"face"}}],"params":{"sketchId":"sk1","distance":10.0,"extrudeMode":"Blind","booleanMode":"NewBody"}},{"opType":"Fillet","opId":"op2","stepIndex":2,"inputs":[{"primary":{"bodyId":"body_op1","elementId":"el_edge_v","kind":"edge"},"anchor":{"worldPoint":[0,0,5]}}],"params":{"mode":"Fillet","radius":2.0,"edgeIds":["el_edge_v"],"chainTangentEdges":true,"tangentClosureVersion":1,"targetBodyId":"body_op1"}}]}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"event","id":2,"event":"planStep","stepIndex":0,"jobId":31,"payload":{"bodyEvents":[]}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"event","id":2,"event":"planStep","stepIndex":1,"jobId":31,"payload":{"bodyEvents":[{"kind":"created","bodyId":"body_op1"}]}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"event","id":2,"event":"planStep","stepIndex":2,"jobId":31,"payload":{"bodyEvents":[{"kind":"modified","bodyId":"body_op1"}]}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"resp","id":2,"ok":true,"jobId":31,"result":{"planPrepared":true,"lastValidStep":2,"stoppedReason":"completed"}}}
{"send":{"v":1,"t":"req","id":3,"verb":"AcceptPrepared","args":{"jobId":31,"documentRevision":1,"workerEpoch":4}}}
